                \/
                %strong pseudofunctor
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-functor"} n-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functor"} (∞,n)-functor
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of pseudo-functors from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            originates with:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              , §A.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Technique de descente et théorèmes d’existence en géométrie algébrique. I. Généralités. Descente par morphismes fidèlement plats
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+Bourbaki"} N. Bourbaki
              exp. no190 (1960) 299-327 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SB_1958-1960__5__299_0"}> numdam:SB_1958-1960__5__299_0
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            (where it is still called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+categories"}> fibered categories
            ”, a term that eventually came to refer to the
            %a{:href => "Grothendieck+construction#EquivalenceBetweenFiberedCategoriesAndPsuedofunctors"} equivalent incarnation
            of pseudofunctors as their
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+constructions"} Grothendieck constructions
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angelo+Vistoli"}> Angelo Vistoli
              , Def. 3.10 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck topologies, fibered categories and descent theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fundamental+algebraic+geometry+--+Grothendieck%27s+FGA+explained"} Fundamental algebraic geometry – Grothendieck's FGA explained
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 123
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-123-s"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4245-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0412512"} math.AG/0412512
          %p
            The general notion of pseudo-functors between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            is introduced as
            %strong homomorphisms of bicategories
            in:
          %ul
            %li#Ben
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to Bicategories
              %strong 47
              Springer (1967), pp.1-77 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BFb0074299"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0074299
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            In the above,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+pseudofunctors"} strict pseudofunctors
            are called
            %strong strict homomorphisms of bicategories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functors"} lax functors
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong morphisms of bicategories
          %ul
            %li#JohnsonYau20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %em 2-Dimensional Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://oxford.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001/oso-9780198871378"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001
          %p See also:
          %ul#LP
            %li#Lack
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Codescent objects and coherence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/journal/00224049/175/1"} web
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"} Stephen Lack
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simona+Paoli"} Simona Paoli
                = succeed "-Theory" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                = succeed ")." do
